% expect-output: 12.0
% expect-output: 0.0
% expect-output: 136.0
% expect-output: 100.0
% Scenario: a scale before setcachedevice. The glyph procedure halves
% the coordinate system and then declares width 1200 and box
% 0 0 1200 1200 in that space, so in glyph space the width is 600 and
% the box 0 0 600 600: at size 20 each glyph advances 12, stringwidth
% agrees with show, and the captured glyph's line reads 600 and
% [0 0 600 600] with the triangle inside it.
% Expect: 12.0 0.0, then 136.0 100.0.
/r { 1000 mul round 1000 div } def
/Tri 7 dict dup begin
  /FontType 3 def
  /FontMatrix [0.001 0 0 0.001 0 0] def
  /Encoding StandardEncoding def
  /FontBBox [0 0 600 600] def
  /BuildGlyph {
    pop pop
    0.5 0.5 scale
    1200 0 0 0 1200 1200 setcachedevice
    0 0 moveto 1200 0 lineto 600 1200 lineto closepath fill
  } def
end definefont pop
/Tri findfont 20 scalefont setfont
(a) stringwidth r exch r = =
100 100 moveto (aaa) show currentpoint r exch r = =
showpage
